<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taejo of Joseon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1335–1408</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Yi Seong-gye</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taejo of Joseon, born Yi Seong-gye, was a Goryeo general who won fame fighting Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> and Red Turban invaders. Ordered to attack Ming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 1388, he turned his army back at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wihwa-island">Wihwa Island</a> and took control of the government. In 1392 he deposed the last Goryeo king and founded the Joseon dynasty, moving the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Hanyang</a> (Seoul).</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taejo-of-joseon.jpg" alt="Taejo of Joseon" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jo Jung-muk(?-?), Pak Gijun(?-?), Baek Eunbae(1820-?), Yu Suk(1827-1873) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Taejo_Yi_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
